<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Massagetae</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 100 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful nomadic confederation east of the Caspian, best known for Queen Tomyris, whose warriors defeated and killed Cyrus the Great in 530 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Greek historians, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, describe the Massagetae living beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a>, usually identified with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>, on the plains east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a> from the 6th century BCE. They were related to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/saka">Saka</a> and are often treated as one of the major Saka groupings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> describes a people fighting both on horseback and on foot with bows, lances and bronze-headed battle-axes, using gold and bronze but no iron or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>. They worshipped the sun, to which they sacrificed horses, and lived on herds and fish. Some groups occupied the deltas of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a>, near the farming towns of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-khwarazm">Kingdom of Khwarazm</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After their victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus</a>, the Massagetae fade from detailed record. They are mentioned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great's</a> campaigns in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-samarkand">Sogdiana</a>, then dissolve into later steppe groupings, among them the peoples displaced by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a>. Their name was later revived by Byzantine writers as a learned label for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 600 BCE – 100 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:47.76%;width:9.95%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 100 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tomyris</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iranian steppe religion, sun worship</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Eastern Iranian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a>, <a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Massagetai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-350&amp;focus=massagetae" aria-label="Massagetae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6272 474 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Massagetae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6592 730h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6592 730h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Kazakhstan. <a href="/atlas?year=-350&amp;focus=massagetae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

